      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓⲍ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="3">The editors note: not ⲉⲕⲁⲧⲥⲉⲃⲁⲛ (apparatus).</p>
        <p n="7">Measured stroke 778–798 over ⲙⲛ (in the restoration): it covers ⲛ 57 % and ⲙ 47 %, so it is encoded on ⲛ only.</p>
        <p n="12">The last bracket is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="13">A raised ink blot between the second and third dot is a printing speck and is not encoded.</p>
        <p n="21">Measured overline 846–905: it covers ⲭⲥ and not ⲛ (40 %).</p>
        <p n="23">The editors print "geringe Spuren" (slight traces); no text is given.</p>
        <p n="24">Lines 24–25: the editors print, with a brace over both lines, "abgerieben" (rubbed off); no text is given.</p>
        <p n="25">See l. 24.</p>
        <p n="28">Lines 28–29: the editors print, with a brace over both lines, "geringe Spuren" (slight traces); no text is given.</p>
        <p n="29">See l. 28.</p>
        <p n="35">The editors print the end of the word, ⲗⲱⲥ̣, below the line end (turnover); it is part of this line. They call [ⲧⲱ]ⲕ ⲁⲣⲉⲧⲟⲩ quite uncertain (apparatus).</p>
      </div>
